comments.body:
Manually deleting the registry key that [the installer checks](https://github.com/podman-container-tools/podman/blob/e1ddac9c0a889245f6438c1149ac05ee0762fa0f/contrib/win-installer/wix/podman-main.wxs#L28-L33) (HKLM\SOFTWARE\Red Hat\Podman) solved the problem so there isn't much we can do here: the new podman installer (msi) never uninstalls the old installer (setup.exe). Podman Desktop does that automatically, though. 

In your case, I suspect the uninstallation failed for some reason, and the registry key wasn't deleted. Podman Desktop should have noticed the failure and aborted the installation of the new version of Podman. This is only speculation, but there isn't enough information ([uninstallation logs](https://github.com/podman-container-tools/podman/blob/v5.3/build_windows.md?plain=1#L470), version of the old Podman) to investigate, and I cannot reproduce it locally (if I install and then uninstall the old Podman v5.3.2, the registry key causing the problem is always deleted).

@QBos07 I am closing this issue because there isn't enough information to work on it, but feel free to reopen it if you can provide the missing info.
